- How would you test header-driven routing in CI?
- How would you add health checks and a safe rollback?

## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates practical secret lifecycle management in Docker Swarm, integrating Vault for automated rotation with zero-downtime upgrades and proper secret versioning.

## Key Concepts
- Swarm secrets versioning and dynamic reattachment
- Vault-based rotation triggers and secret provisioning
- Rolling updates with start-first strategy to avoid downtime
- Health checks to confirm new secrets are loaded before removing old ones
- Atomic secret updates using add-then-remove pattern

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-automation: rotate Vault-derived Swarm secrets
async function rotateSecrets(serviceName, vaultPath) {
  // Fetch new credentials from Vault
  const newCreds = await vault.read(vaultPath);

  // Create new Swarm secrets
  const newSecrets = await createSwarmSecrets(newCreds);

  // Update service with new secrets
  await updateService(serviceName, newSecrets);

  // Verify health before cleanup
  await verifyServiceHealth(serviceName);

  // Remove old secrets
  await cleanupOldSecrets(serviceName);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to wire config-driven per-tenant controls in a multi-DC docker-dca setup, with TLS edge and simple runtime enforcement.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config for runtime limits
- Per-tenant rate limiting (token bucket)
- TLS via Traefik edge proxy
- Basic cross-DC deployment considerations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: token bucket per tenant with 60 rpm
const limits = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/etc/config/tenant-rate-limits.json','utf8'));
const buckets = new Map();
function allow(tenant){
  const now = Date.now();
  let b = buckets.get(tenant);
  if(!b){ b = {tokens: limits[tenant]||0, last: now}; buckets.set(tenant,b); }
  // simplistic: refill 1 token per second for 60s window
  const elapsed = (now - b.last)/1000; b.last = now; b.tokens = Math.min((limits[tenant]||0), b.tokens + elapsed);
  if(b.tokens >= 1){ b.tokens--; return true; }
  return false;
}
```

